CONCEPT
  product:   Squab — employer of record for feral and semi-feral avian labour
  one-liner: global payroll, benefits and worker classification for birds that
             do not recognise your borders
  The joke sits on worker misclassification: the birds on your roof are already
  engaged workers and you are already the employer. Features are Ledge Audit,
  Grain Settlement and Statutory Molt Leave. Testimonials run one registered
  bird and two panicking employers.

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style:   vitreous enamel border-formalities signage, arrivals-hall dark mode
  palette: bg #0D2B22 (bottle green) / carrier #EFE7D2 (enamel bone) /
           rationed #D6452F (customs vermilion, non-compliance only) /
           muted #8CA79A
  fonts:   display Chivo 900, body Literata, telemetry JetBrains Mono
  motifs:  the double-keyline enamel plate, the leg band (999px capsule with a
           worker ID), the rotated vermilion declaration stamp

  Anti-sameness check against the last 7 entries (cursor-for-crows cyanotype
  blueprint, medium-for-remote-workers vellum manuscript, spacex trophy case,
  medium-for-doomscrollers pharma blister, fortnite claymorphic launcher,
  tesla-for-perpetual-interns aurora glass, vercel-for-guys-named-steve 1974
  supergraphic manual): no collision on style, palette or font pair. Bottle
  green as a *ground* is new (prior darks were navy, black and slate; the two
  prior greens were marks on light grounds). Chivo + Literata is unused.

IMAGES  (4 generated, 4 kept, 0 dropped, 0 retries)
  rationale:
    hero        — skipped. The direction is typographic signage; a photograph
                  would be a second voice on the sign.
    demo        — 3 images. The console is a worker-ID roster, which is
                  photo-shaped. bird-1/2/3 cycle across the twelve roster rows
                  and the detail drawer.
    testimonial — 1 image. bird-4 is the ID photo for Ferdinand Two-Ring, the
                  only registered worker of the three quoted. The two human
                  employers deliberately get a "no band on file" CSS well
                  instead of a headshot, so the presence of a photo encodes who
                  is actually on a band.
